i07.md:occ-a96bf8b26dea","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci07.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"The BCO provides no minimum voting age for congregational meetings, except where state law imposes one for corporate votes."}},{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Psiaki v. Pacific Northwest Presbytery","year":2024,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-0ec565972f98","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":167},"excerpt":"…draws the same conclusion about the right of minor communicants to vote from BCO 25-1, which does not include the phrase \"in good and regular standing,\" as he does from BCO 24-3, which does include that phrase, underscores the fact that he did not…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"},{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-f4537c2e10b9","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":167},"excerpt":"Smith makes the same point in his commentary on BCO 25-1: \"The voting membership of the congregation is here defined. Note that all communicant members are entitled to vote. Thus, when young children are admitted to the Table on the basis of their profession…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"},{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-374f59ea1b79","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":351},"excerpt":"BCO 25-1 is, we believe, misunderstood to grant universal entitlement to vote for all communicant members. BCO 25-1 says, “The congregation consists of all the communing members of a particular church, and they only are entitled to vote.\" Because this…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"},{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-89fcc2440865","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":351},"excerpt":"…to grant universal entitlement to vote for all communicant members. BCO 25-1 says, “The congregation consists of all the communing members of a particular church, and they only are entitled to vote.\" Because this provision contains the phrase…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"},{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-1d6f933a5e56","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":355},"excerpt":"tempting to interpret this provision as a full grant of voting entitlement, but this is not the case. In fact, the opposite is the case because BCO 25-1, properly understood, is a limit rather than a grant of voting entitlement.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"},{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-8162f59c0488","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":357},"excerpt":"BCO 25-1 was added by the PCUS in 1925 together with the entire chapter now governing \"Congregational Meetings.\" Before 1925, the Form of Government had no independent section regulating congregational meetings or generally addressing the corporate aspects of…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"},{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-353c53834307","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":359},"excerpt":"…standing” expressly prescribed in BCO 20-3 and 24-3 is entirely unaffected by BCO 25-1, which effectively provides that being a communicant member is a necessary but not a sufficient qualification to vote at a congregational meeting. In other words, unlike…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"},{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md:occ-fd9599a0031a","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":359},"excerpt":"Moreover, taken on its face, BCO 25-1 does not say that all communicant members of a congregation are unqualifiedly entitled to vote; it states merely that \"they only,\" meaning communing members, are entitled to vote. The regulation or restriction of voting…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-11.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["minor communicant voting","congregational meeting","voting rights","good and regular standing","church bylaws","officer election","communicant membership","BCO 6-4","BCO 20-3","BCO 24-3","BCO 25-1","age restrictions","session authority"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2023-11"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The SJC sustained Psiaki’s complaint and held that the CPC Session erred by ordaining and installing officers elected at a February 5, 2023 congregational meeting where the congregation’s bylaw excluded communing members under 18 from voting. Reading BCO 6-4, 25-1, and 25-7 together, the SJC ruled that all communing members are entitled to vote and that local bylaws cannot impose an age restriction; the “good and regular standing” language addresses censure, not age. The decision did not annul the completed ordination/installation, but required future elections and installations to comply with the Constitution."}},{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Wilson et al. v. Pacific Northwest Presbytery","year":2023,"disposition":"dismissed","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md:occ-eccbf54259ce","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.html","repository_path":"cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":465},"excerpt":"BCO 25-1. The congregation consists of all the communing members of a particular church, and they only are entitled to vote.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md"},{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md:occ-b6156bb7261b","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.html","repository_path":"cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":469},"excerpt":"…consists of all the lions of a particular region, and they only birth lions.\" BCO 25-1 no more states that all communicants are entitled to vote, than the latter implies that all lions are female. Again, “those only who are Olympic athletes are entitled to…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md"},{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md:occ-f222afe45224","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.html","repository_path":"cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":469},"excerpt":"Simple substitution examples for those two BCO passages render the point clear. BCO 25-1 is equivalent to the statement: “The pride consists of all the lions of a particular region, and they only birth lions.\" BCO 25-1 no more states that all communicants are…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md"},{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md:occ-193e254b8197","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.html","repository_path":"cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":696},"excerpt":"…it should be said that the “General Assembly acted wisely\" when it adopted BCO 25-1, “without legislating on the specific matter\" of a minimum voting age.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md"},{"id":"bco:25-1--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md:occ-bf8581d46d8e","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.html","repository_path":"cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":698},"excerpt":"…of a minimum voting age. A novice reader may develop the impression from BCO 25-1 that every communicant is entitled to vote. However, a capable minister will be able to explain the difference between a necessary and sufficient condition. He will also…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["congregational meeting","minor communicant suffrage","voting rights","communing members","church bylaws","BCO 43-1 justiciability","associate pastor resignation","Covenant Presbyterian Church","Pacific Northwest Presbytery"],"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2022-20"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Members challenged a voting restriction imposed at a congregational meeting. The SJC dismissed the complaint as judicially out of order because BCO 43-1 permits complaints against acts or decisions of church courts, and a congregation is not such a court. It identified other possible routes through a report to Presbytery or review of church records. The adopted decision did not decide whether the voting restriction was constitutionally valid."}},{"id":"bco:25-1--overture:ga52_2025:22","record_id":"overture:ga52_2025:22","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 20-3, 24-3, and 25-1 to Permit Congregational Minimum Voting Age","year":2025,"disposition":"Answered in the negative","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga52_2025.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga52_2025.md","evidence_basis":"overture_action_target","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:25-1--overture:ga52_2025:22:occ-557cb3963e36","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga52_2025.html#ga52-p1208","repository_path":"markdown/ga52_2025.md#ga52-p1208","locator":{"fragment":"ga52-p1208","page":1208},"excerpt":"","sources":["disposition_bco"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga52_2025.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"source":"OVERTURE 22 from the Pacific Northwest Presbytery (to CCB, OC)"}},{"id":"bco:25-1--overture:ga52_2025:13","record_id":"overture:ga52_2025:13","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 25-1 to Limit Voting to Members in Good Standing","year":2025,"disposition":"Answered in the negative","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url"